<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Torrellas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1304</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Torrellas was an arbitration of 8 August 1304, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denis-rapontchombo">King Denis</a> of Portugal, that settled the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and Aragon over the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>. Aragon kept the northern part of Murcia, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alicante">Alicante</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elche">Elche</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orihuela">Orihuela</a>, while Castile kept the rest. The line, adjusted by the Treaty of Elche in 1305, fixed the southern border of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-torrellas.jpg" alt="Treaty of Torrellas" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DaniCBP · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_Divisi%C3%B3n_del_Reino_de_Murcia_-_Sentencia_de_Torrellas_y_Tratado_de_Elche.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
